Noto Sans Syriac is an unmodulated (sans serif) Estrangela design for
texts in the Middle Eastern Syriac script. It is the design used for
Classical Syriac, and for headings and titles in West and East Syriac
text. It also covers Arabic and Latin characters.

This package installs the complete upstream font set, not the reduced
Google Fonts subset, under /usr/share/fonts/TTF:

  NotoSansSyriac-Thin.ttf, NotoSansSyriac-Regular.ttf,
  NotoSansSyriac-Black.ttf, and the variable font
  NotoSansSyriac[wght].ttf.

The static fonts cover the Thin, Regular, and Black weights. The
variable font adds the ExtraLight, Light, Medium, SemiBold, Bold, and
ExtraBold weights through a weight axis running from 100 to 900.

The fonts are licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1. The
license text is in /usr/doc/ttf-noto-sans-syriac-<version>/.
